# oracle: w300neb_efirst_middle — LAMMPS examples/neb in.neb.hop1 on 4 replicas with quickmin, a perpendicular spring (perp) and end last/efirst/middle (the last replica's target energy is the first replica's current energy; an intermediate replica below it loses its gradient force), the verbose table
# oracle-partitions: 4
# oracle-examples: neb/initial.hop1 neb/final.hop1
# oracle-compare: rel=1e-4 abs=1e-6
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (NEB table): 2.9e-6 in the columns printed with 8 significant digits, 4.8e-5 in the verbose columns (5 significant digits).
# The hop1 path interpolated over 4 or 5 replicas starts with overlapping atoms and quickmin amplifies rounding: a 1e-13 displacement of the engine's own input grows to 1e-7 by step 80 and to order 1 by step 135, so the case stops before that. Measured with native LAMMPS: min_style fire on this path ends in a segmentation fault.
dimension       2
boundary        p s p
atom_style      atomic
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 5
atom_modify     map array sort 0 0.0
variable        u uloop 20
lattice         hex 0.9
region          box block 0 20 0 10 -0.25 0.25
read_data       initial.hop1
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
pair_modify     shift yes
region          1 block INF INF INF 1.25 INF INF
group           lower region 1
group           mobile subtract all lower
set             group lower type 2
timestep        0.05
region          surround block 10 18 17 20 0 0 units box
group           nebatoms region surround
set             group nebatoms type 3
group           nonneb subtract all nebatoms
fix             1 lower setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
fix             2 nebatoms neb 1.0 perp 1.0 end last/efirst/middle 1.0
fix             3 all enforce2d
thermo          100
min_style       quickmin
neb             0.0 0.05 50 30 10 final final.hop1 verbosity verbose
